L wrote:
> Chakram sounds like it'd be an entire skill slot to itself, if you ask
> me.

Sounds like an excellent reason to introduce another new item: The
Frisbee (tm). Shows up as a tool, but if you throw it at a monster it
can do up to 1HP damage. Playing with frisbees can excercise the
chakram skill.

Tame (small|large) dogs will always run towards any frisbee thrown by
any monster. This allows you to 'guide' the pet toward a monster or
other objective, but it also allows iIntelligent monsters to throw
frisbees to one side and distract incoming dogs.

Tame dogs will happily step onto the same square as a cursed frisbee.
Pet dogs will always pick up frisbees in the same square as them- in
fact the only thing they are more interested in is food.

Tame and peaceful dogs will attempt to catch a frisbee thrown at them
by the player. The chances of succes are listed further down this post.

If the catch is successful, the player excercises the Chakram skill.
If unsuccessful, the frisbee strikes the dog and counts as an attack
(up to 1HP damage, lost tameness, peaceful->hostile as appropriate).

You can also play frisbee with other pets: Anything capable of wielding
a weapon (ie humanoid pets) is capable of catching a frisbee. They
won't chase them, but they will try to catch frisbees thrown directly
at them. The player gets the same rewards and penalties for
caught/fumbled frisbees.

When a tame dog is carrying a blessed fisbee: Dog will return to the
player's feet (ie adjacent square) and immediately drop the frisbee.

When a tame dog is carrying an uncursed fisbee: Dog has same likelihood
of dropping the frisbee as it would any normal item.

When a tame dog is carrying a cursed frisbee: The dog will be very
reluctant to drop the frisbee. It will only drop the frisbee when (a)
it is polymorphed into something else or (b) it is dead or (c) it is
hungry and drops the frisbee to eat. This can really hamper
shoplifting.

Peaceful dogs who have caught a frisbee will drop it immediately and
carry on with whatever they were doing.

Non-dog pets holding frisbees will throw them to the player, with the
same chances of catch/fumble as above. Catches excercise dexterity and
the Chakram skill. fumbled catches risk HP loss. This introduce
YApossible gravestone message:
"Killed in a friendly game of catch".

Blessed frisbees start with a 90% base chance of being caught.
Uncursed ones start with a 50% chance..
Cursed ones start with a 10% chance.
Gauntlets of fumbling worn by either the thrower or catcher reduce the
base chances of success to 1% in all cases.
The base chance is then subjected to the modifiers below:.
Gloves worn by the catcher introduce a -5% modifer.
Gloves worn by the thrower introduce a (further) -5% modifer.
Body armour worn by the catcher introduces a (further) -10% modifer.
Finally, the player's luck and dex modify the result even further.

Shopkeepers will not buy frisbees (too easy to credit clone with dogs,
otherwise). Tourists who start with a dog have a 30% chance of getting
a frisbee.

It would be nice if NPC orcs/goblins could be made to play frisbee with
wargs as well, but I imagine that would be a bitch to code.

A patch like this one would also open the possibility of playing
"fetch" using quarterstaves or wands, but one thing at a time, eh?



